Package: proof
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Charles Pickering <me@charlespick.xyz>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1 | libgcc1, libstdc++6, libssl3t64 | libssl3 | libssl1.1, ca-certificates, init-system-helpers
Recommends: hyperv-daemons | linux-cloud-tools-virtual
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/charlespick/Proof
Description: Hyper-V VM identity client
 proof reads the host token that the Hyper-V host writes into this VM over
 KVP, trades it with the Proof issuer for an audience-specific JWT, and
 prints the JWT or writes it to a file.
 .
 It reads the KVP pool that hv_kvp_daemon keeps, and its settings from
 /etc/proof/config.json, which the image provides.
 .
 proof-metadata is a service on 127.0.0.1:8169 that serves the OpenStack
 instance metadata API to cloud-init from the Hyper-V host and the VM's Hyper-V
 notes. It needs the hv_sock kernel module.
 .
 It also installs Proof, a cloud-init data source for that API, which the
 image's cloud-init config turns on.
